{
  "rule": "weno5_advection",
  "applicable": false,
  "skip_reason": "Layer-A canonical drive of `weno5_advection` requires ESS `discretize`/`parse_rule` to dispatch the FV `applies_to` schema (rather than the `pattern` schema it currently consumes). The catalog rule pairs `applies_to: div(*(U, q), dim=$x)` with a closed §4.2 `arrayop` `replacement` expression that lowers div(U·q) on a uniform 1D Cartesian grid to the Jiang-Shu (1996) WENO5 face-flux form (eqs. 2.5-2.10 and 2.16-2.18) plus an upwind ifelse on the cell-to-face-averaged U. ESS `rule_engine.jl::parse_rule` rejects non-`pattern` rule entries (E_RULE_REPLACEMENT_MISSING / pattern key missing), so the catalog rule cannot be materialized end-to-end via the canonical pipeline yet. Once ESS gains `applies_to`-schema dispatch, this stub can be promoted to a hand-pinned canonical contract on a small periodic 1D grid (e.g. N=16 cells, U(x) = 1, q(x) = sin(2*pi*x)) byte-pinned against the canonicalized `discretize` output of a model whose RHS is `div(U*q, dim=x)`.",
  "reference_implementation": {
    "module": "EarthSciDiscretizations",
    "function": "weno5_advection_arrayop (catalog rule replacement)",
    "path": "discretizations/finite_volume/weno5_advection.json",
    "comment": "The catalog rule's `replacement` is the closed arrayop AST that materializes the WENO5 face-flux update at every interior cell on a 1D periodic grid. Smoothness indicators beta_k (Shu 1998 eq. 2.17), nonlinear weights alpha_k = d_k / (eps + beta_k)^2 (Jiang-Shu eqs. 2.9-2.10), and the convex combination omega_k * p_k are all expressed as +, -, *, /, ^ over `index` selectors. Layer-B convergence on this rule SKIPs pending the canonical-pipeline replacement of the retired ESS verify_mms_convergence (esm-4t5)."
  },
